null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4.1\n\n### System information\n\nDoesn't matter\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen you add a new SkeletonModification2DTwoBoneIK to the modification stack of a Skeleton2D it starts printing the followint error until you change the value of its `joint_one_bone_idx`, you don't even need to enable the stack:\n\"ERROR: [scene/2d/skeleton_2d.cpp:625](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/c81fd6c51233a727da528cf7f74137d56b5d6efe/scene/2d/skeleton_2d.cpp#L625) - Index p_idx = -1 is out of bounds ((int)bones.size() = 0).\"\nAnd since it does it every frame, it can drastically reduce your performance, which can even prevent you from changing the value (if the editor FPS becomes too low).\nAnd obviously the engine should not print errors when you did nothing wrong (which is, I believe, the case, because just adding a new modificaion is a part of the normal Skeleton2D workflow).\n\n\n\n<img width=\"1538\" height=\"926\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e071b493-d1b7-4b09-8ebb-1a8bc37f7a31\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a Skeleton2D node\n2. Add a new modification stack to it\n3. Add a new SkeletonModification2DTwoBoneIK\n4. Enjoy thousands of errors in your debug console and low FPS\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[skeleton-2d-issue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21614753/skeleton-2d-issue.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"ht